1
00:00:03,130 --> 00:00:05,550
This is our starting lineup.

2
00:00:06,090 --> 00:00:08,840
We'll approach the France match with man-to-man marking.

3
00:00:08,920 --> 00:00:12,760
We'll press high against forward Napoleon and midfielder Pierre.

4
00:00:12,840 --> 00:00:14,640
Soda, you take Napoleon.

5
00:00:14,720 --> 00:00:15,560
Yes.

6
00:00:15,640 --> 00:00:17,220
We trust you, forward hunter.

7
00:00:17,310 --> 00:00:19,230
Yes, leave it to me.

8
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:21,480
Misaki, you mark Pierre.

9
00:00:21,730 --> 00:00:22,850
I trust you.

10
00:00:22,940 --> 00:00:23,770
Yes.

11
00:00:24,020 --> 00:00:24,980
Misaki-kun.

12
00:00:25,520 --> 00:00:28,110
Now it's time to settle everything with Pierre.

13
00:00:28,900 --> 00:00:30,110
Wakashimazu.

14
00:00:31,530 --> 00:00:34,950
Napoleon's shot has a special spin.

15
00:00:35,030 --> 00:00:37,490
If you try to catch it with your palm, it'll slip out of your hands.

16
00:00:38,120 --> 00:00:39,870
Yes, I know.

17
00:00:43,210 --> 00:00:44,920
Why, Wakabayashi?

18
00:00:45,340 --> 00:00:48,760
We beat Argentina, but I still conceded 4 goals.

19
00:00:49,460 --> 00:00:52,470
Why aren't you playing in this match?

20
00:00:53,510 --> 00:00:58,930
You should take back your spot, so why are you still leaving the goal to me?

21
00:01:00,140 --> 00:01:03,270
Alright guys, let's show them our strength!

22
00:01:03,350 --> 00:01:04,770
Yes.

23
00:01:07,820 --> 00:01:11,150
Let's do this! This is the semifinal!

24
00:01:21,790 --> 00:01:26,670
CAPTAIN TSUBASA: JUNIOR YOUTH ARC

25
00:02:42,480 --> 00:02:48,320
EPISODE 20
THE BATTLE BEGINS!! JAPAN - FRANCE

26
00:02:44,900 --> 00:02:47,070
Alright, it's started.

27
00:02:47,150 --> 00:02:48,320
Finally.

28
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:51,320
Tsubasa-senpai, come to the field quickly.

29
00:02:51,410 --> 00:02:53,530
Sorry, we disturbed you late with so many people.

30
00:02:53,620 --> 00:02:57,410
It's fine, the more we are, the more fun it is.

31
00:02:57,500 --> 00:02:59,460
Finally our players are entering the field.

32
00:02:59,620 --> 00:03:02,080
Good luck! France!

33
00:03:02,170 --> 00:03:03,880
You have to win!

34
00:03:03,960 --> 00:03:05,750
Don't lose to Japan!

35
00:03:05,840 --> 00:03:08,210
Napoleon, let's win this match with 3 hat-tricks.

36
00:03:08,460 --> 00:03:12,550
Host France may have the upper hand in cheering,

37
00:03:12,640 --> 00:03:15,100
but no one can predict the result.

38
00:03:15,180 --> 00:03:18,520
Will it be Japan or France as the finalist?

39
00:03:18,600 --> 00:03:19,730
Tsubasa-kun.

40
00:03:22,190 --> 00:03:25,190
Damn it, they outnumber us.

41
00:03:25,900 --> 00:03:29,990
And those kids are supporting France instead of Misaki.

42
00:03:30,240 --> 00:03:32,740
Woooow, I'm very disappointed.

43
00:03:34,410 --> 00:03:36,740
Captains, time to shake hands.

44
00:03:37,040 --> 00:03:38,160
- Good luck.
- Good luck.

45
00:03:42,460 --> 00:03:44,500
Japan - France

46
00:03:44,790 --> 00:03:47,670
Both teams have taken their places.

47
00:03:47,750 --> 00:03:50,590
The second semifinal match is about to begin.

48
00:03:50,670 --> 00:03:55,600
Germany beat Uruguay in the first match and advanced to the final.

49
00:03:55,800 --> 00:03:57,640
The match begins with France's kickoff.

50
00:03:58,390 --> 00:04:03,440
Who will win and advance to the final? Japan or France?

51
00:04:04,850 --> 00:04:09,360
First, the ball is at the feet of captain El Sid Pierre.

52
00:04:09,480 --> 00:04:12,360
- Great, this is Pierre.
- How handsome! Pierre!

53
00:04:13,030 --> 00:04:14,610
Bring it on, Pierre.

54
00:04:14,780 --> 00:04:16,620
Misaki-kun pairs up with him.

55
00:04:16,780 --> 00:04:18,620
Come on, Misaki!

56
00:04:18,790 --> 00:04:19,910
Misaki.

57
00:04:20,080 --> 00:04:21,450
Take this!

58
00:04:21,540 --> 00:04:24,000
Hyuga-kun tries to steal the ball with a tackle.

59
00:04:24,870 --> 00:04:27,000
Pierre escapes with a leap.

60
00:04:27,460 --> 00:04:29,630
Now Misaki-kun also jumps.

61
00:04:29,880 --> 00:04:32,010
Both have equal strength.

62
00:04:32,420 --> 00:04:33,760
This is just like those times.

63
00:04:35,800 --> 00:04:37,680
The ball separated from him.

64
00:04:37,760 --> 00:04:39,350
- Misaki.
- Pierre!

65
00:04:39,510 --> 00:04:42,980
Oh! Tsubasa-kun gets it in the air!

66
00:04:43,730 --> 00:04:44,640
Tsubasa-kun!

67
00:04:44,730 --> 00:04:45,850
Great, Tsubasa!

68
00:04:46,060 --> 00:04:50,110
Hyuga-kun, Misaki-kun, and Tsubasa-kun attacked as a trio.

69
00:04:50,320 --> 00:04:54,610
And they snatched the ball from France's support pillar Pierre.

70
00:04:54,740 --> 00:04:57,120
Great, advance Japan!

71
00:04:57,570 --> 00:04:58,660
Tsubasa!

72
00:04:58,870 --> 00:05:00,740
Pierre lost the ball.

73
00:05:00,830 --> 00:05:03,040
This has never happened before.

74
00:05:03,160 --> 00:05:04,870
Then we'll take it back.

75
00:05:04,960 --> 00:05:06,040
Crush him.

76
00:05:06,460 --> 00:05:09,040
France presses Tsubasa-kun.

77
00:05:10,090 --> 00:05:11,420
During the Argentina match,

78
00:05:11,500 --> 00:05:14,970
Roberto being in the stands distracted me and I made a mistake.

79
00:05:15,840 --> 00:05:19,050
But the first thing Roberto taught me was dribbling.

80
00:05:24,350 --> 00:05:25,810
Alright kids.

81
00:05:26,020 --> 00:05:28,230
When we return to the hotel, pack your bags.

82
00:05:28,310 --> 00:05:30,110
We must go home immediately.

83
00:05:30,190 --> 00:05:31,770
Okay.

84
00:05:34,690 --> 00:05:37,070
Excuse me, stop the bus.

85
00:05:41,120 --> 00:05:43,660
Coach Ramirez, I entrust the team to you.

86
00:05:43,750 --> 00:05:45,580
I'm returning to Brazil with tomorrow's flight.

87
00:05:45,910 --> 00:05:48,330
- What?
- Coach Roberto!

88
00:05:48,620 --> 00:05:52,170
Tsubasa-kun tries to get past with an attacking dribble.

89
00:05:52,670 --> 00:05:57,010
He seemed to push through by force, but now he's using his technique.

90
00:05:57,090 --> 00:05:59,260
He passes the French players like a whirlwind.

91
00:06:00,390 --> 00:06:01,760
Great, Tsubasa.

92
00:06:02,430 --> 00:06:05,810
For good dribbling, always think two or three steps ahead of the opponent.

93
00:06:05,890 --> 00:06:12,610
And this requires constant balance and secure ball control.

94
00:06:12,980 --> 00:06:15,030
That's what Roberto said.

95
00:06:15,740 --> 00:06:18,280
He advances the ball well, as usual.

96
00:06:18,570 --> 00:06:21,780
Can't you even stop a dribble like this?

97
00:06:21,990 --> 00:06:24,790
I, the Great Napoleon, will stop him.

98
00:06:25,200 --> 00:06:28,120
Napoleon-kun attacks quickly!

99
00:06:28,210 --> 00:06:29,540
Be careful, Tsubasa-kun!

100
00:06:30,210 --> 00:06:31,540
Catch, here it comes.

101
00:06:33,250 --> 00:06:34,920
Tsubasa-kun passes back!

102
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:36,170
That damn...

103
00:06:37,670 --> 00:06:40,180
The ball goes directly to Misaki-kun.

104
00:06:40,760 --> 00:06:42,970
Tsubasa-kun repositions.

105
00:06:43,220 --> 00:06:45,810
Pierre-kun goes after Misaki-kun.

106
00:06:48,270 --> 00:06:51,600
Oh, Misaki-kun didn't hold the ball, he passed to the corner.

107
00:06:51,690 --> 00:06:53,150
Nice.

108
00:06:53,860 --> 00:06:54,900
Misaki.

109
00:06:55,360 --> 00:06:59,990
We're going to the final, our individual duel has to wait.

110
00:07:00,530 --> 00:07:03,120
The ball goes to Soda-kun on the overlap.

111
00:07:03,200 --> 00:07:06,540
We will beat Germany, the strongest team in the cup.

112
00:07:08,370 --> 00:07:12,080
Is this the final pass to Tsubasa-kun running in front of the goal?

113
00:07:12,170 --> 00:07:13,040
Come on!

114
00:07:13,380 --> 00:07:15,040
I'll catch it, I'll intercept the pass.

115
00:07:16,590 --> 00:07:17,420
What?

116
00:07:17,510 --> 00:07:21,510
This is Soda-kun's special move: a horizontally spinning ball.

117
00:07:21,630 --> 00:07:23,260
Sharp spinning pass.

118
00:07:23,680 --> 00:07:26,640
The ball goes toward Hyuga-kun on the other side.

119
00:07:26,720 --> 00:07:28,180
Great pass, Soda.

120
00:07:28,270 --> 00:07:30,770
He's going to shoot now, watch out.

121
00:07:31,310 --> 00:07:34,480
Tsubasa, I adapted to your Drive Shot.

122
00:07:34,560 --> 00:07:38,530
Now it's your turn to adapt to my Tiger Shot.

123
00:07:39,400 --> 00:07:44,410
We can't lose, we have to settle the score with Germany, Tsubasa.

124
00:07:45,160 --> 00:07:48,290
Tiger Shot!

125
00:07:49,200 --> 00:07:51,750
Hyuga-kun takes his special long-distance shot.

126
00:07:51,830 --> 00:07:53,580
No, the direction is different.

127
00:07:53,670 --> 00:07:56,840
This is the final pass for Tsubasa-kun running in front of the goal.

128
00:07:56,920 --> 00:08:00,760
But can he adapt to the speed of this magnificent pass?

129
00:08:00,920 --> 00:08:02,430
Defense goes to stop him.

130
00:08:02,630 --> 00:08:04,180
No time to control.

131
00:08:04,300 --> 00:08:06,180
Please Tsubasa, you have to score.

132
00:08:06,760 --> 00:08:12,190
When I was a forward in elementary school, Roberto always said:

133
00:08:12,390 --> 00:08:15,310
"Become a midfielder."

134
00:08:15,810 --> 00:08:18,070
The goal-scoring skill I had as a forward,

135
00:08:18,150 --> 00:08:21,610
I must also keep in my midfielder position.

136
00:08:21,690 --> 00:08:25,200
I must be a midfielder who can both direct play and score goals.

137
00:08:25,490 --> 00:08:28,700
Only then will I truly deserve to wear the number 10.

138
00:08:29,080 --> 00:08:30,200
This...

139
00:08:30,500 --> 00:08:34,460
is the ideal player that Roberto and I dreamed of.

140
00:08:37,340 --> 00:08:40,420
Jumping volley shot!

141
00:08:41,460 --> 00:08:43,970
Goal! Incredible!

142
00:08:44,050 --> 00:08:46,010
A magnificent pass came from Hyuga-kun.

143
00:08:46,090 --> 00:08:50,310
And with Ozora Tsubasa-kun's glorious strike, it entered the French goal.

144
00:08:50,720 --> 00:08:52,680
Japan scores the first goal of the match!

145
00:08:52,770 --> 00:08:54,100
No, France...

146
00:08:55,190 --> 00:08:57,310
Great! We did it, guys.

147
00:08:57,440 --> 00:08:59,320
You did it, Tsubasa!

148
00:08:59,400 --> 00:09:01,110
Football wonder.

149
00:09:01,190 --> 00:09:04,820
Japan team's captain Ozora Tsubasa, in top form!

150
00:09:04,900 --> 00:09:05,860
He did it!

151
00:09:05,950 --> 00:09:07,240
Just what you'd expect from Tsubasa.

152
00:09:07,320 --> 00:09:09,830
- Very good.
- He scored from the start.

153
00:09:10,870 --> 00:09:12,200
Tsubasa-kun.

154
00:09:13,160 --> 00:09:15,210
Good, we scored first.

155
00:09:15,370 --> 00:09:18,840
We're against the home team, but we can do it.

156
00:09:19,340 --> 00:09:22,340
Extraordinary, what magnificent harmony.

157
00:09:23,130 --> 00:09:27,640
In the first match, it was Italy's famous goalkeeper Gino Hernandez.

158
00:09:27,800 --> 00:09:30,760
Then it was Argentina's genius Juan Diaz.

159
00:09:30,850 --> 00:09:34,770
Tsubasa Ozora managed to beat both.

160
00:09:35,140 --> 00:09:38,860
And now is he doing the same against France's El Sid Pierre?

161
00:09:39,190 --> 00:09:43,150
Incredible! I will definitely bring him to Argentina.

162
00:09:43,650 --> 00:09:45,900
They scored the first goal.

163
00:09:46,320 --> 00:09:48,450
I guess I have no choice but to show my special shot.

164
00:09:48,530 --> 00:09:50,950
I was keeping it secret.

165
00:09:51,740 --> 00:09:56,910
I planned to save it for the final, but losing is unacceptable.

166
00:09:57,370 --> 00:10:00,170
That number 10 is better than we thought.

167
00:10:01,210 --> 00:10:02,170
Better than me?

168
00:10:03,920 --> 00:10:07,050
So will we face Japan's number 10 in the final?

169
00:10:07,130 --> 00:10:09,010
No, we can't say yet.

170
00:10:09,550 --> 00:10:12,010
France's captain El Sid Pierre.

171
00:10:12,260 --> 00:10:14,770
He used Napoleon very well in this tournament.

172
00:10:14,850 --> 00:10:18,850
And he may have been overshadowed, but he is more than that.

173
00:10:19,020 --> 00:10:21,940
I'm sure he's hiding something.

174
00:10:24,440 --> 00:10:26,440
CAPTAIN TSUBASA: JUNIOR YOUTH ARC

175
00:10:29,760 --> 00:10:31,930
Born: August 16, Height: 171 cm, Weight: 62 kg, Blood Type: B

176
00:10:41,270 --> 00:10:43,810
The match restarts with France's kickoff.

177
00:10:44,110 --> 00:10:47,480
We must win this match.

178
00:10:47,690 --> 00:10:54,240
I will both beat France, and win my duel against you, Misaki.

179
00:10:54,870 --> 00:10:56,030
Pierre.

180
00:10:59,910 --> 00:11:01,250
Napoleon, come on.

181
00:11:06,250 --> 00:11:10,050
I'm coming, I'll make up for the goal we conceded.

182
00:11:10,130 --> 00:11:11,380
Impossible.

183
00:11:12,010 --> 00:11:14,390
Soda-kun is responsible for marking Napoleon-kun.

184
00:11:15,720 --> 00:11:17,850
I'll get past you in three seconds.

185
00:11:17,930 --> 00:11:19,600
Pass the ball back to me.

186
00:11:21,810 --> 00:11:22,640
Napoleon!

187
00:11:22,770 --> 00:11:24,480
Where are you looking?

188
00:11:24,560 --> 00:11:27,400
First it was my spinning sharp pass, now my sharp tackle.

189
00:11:27,480 --> 00:11:28,650
Be careful, Napoleon.

190
00:11:28,980 --> 00:11:30,150
I trust you.

191
00:11:30,360 --> 00:11:31,400
What?

192
00:11:31,570 --> 00:11:36,660
Oh! The force of Soda-kun's tackle is so strong it hits Napoleon-kun's heel.

193
00:11:36,820 --> 00:11:38,660
What the hell are you doing?

194
00:11:39,200 --> 00:11:42,660
The referee plays advantage and Pierre-kun advances with a dribble.

195
00:11:43,500 --> 00:11:46,040
Misaki-kun goes to stop Pierre-kun.

196
00:11:46,460 --> 00:11:48,920
Don't think you'll play comfortably.

197
00:11:49,170 --> 00:11:50,300
I'll stop it right here.

198
00:11:50,460 --> 00:11:52,300
Ishizaki-kun comes to stop him.

199
00:11:53,090 --> 00:11:56,300
Pierre-kun lunges toward Ishizaki-kun.

200
00:11:56,510 --> 00:11:59,310
What is he thinking? I'll catch him.

201
00:12:02,520 --> 00:12:06,980
What a captivating intersection! He glides like a butterfly.

202
00:12:08,110 --> 00:12:11,150
Ishizaki-kun crashes directly into Misaki-kun.

203
00:12:11,360 --> 00:12:13,150
This is Pierre's special move.

204
00:12:13,400 --> 00:12:15,780
I'm showing it to the world for the first time.

205
00:12:15,860 --> 00:12:17,160
This...

206
00:12:21,870 --> 00:12:23,540
My Drive Shot!

207
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:27,920
Pierre-kun takes a long shot.

208
00:12:29,130 --> 00:12:31,920
The ball goes directly toward Japan's goal!

209
00:12:32,010 --> 00:12:35,050
Its path is straight, no spin or rotation.

210
00:12:35,130 --> 00:12:37,550
Slower than the Tiger Shot.

211
00:12:37,680 --> 00:12:38,640
I can catch it.

212
00:12:39,350 --> 00:12:42,560
Goalkeeper Wakashimazu goes to catch it with a dive.

213
00:12:43,730 --> 00:12:44,560
What?

214
00:12:45,560 --> 00:12:47,480
Goal!

215
00:12:47,650 --> 00:12:52,730
It was very close, but it slipped under his hand and went to the right corner.

216
00:12:52,820 --> 00:12:54,190
Wakashimazu!

217
00:12:54,570 --> 00:12:56,320
What was that?

218
00:12:56,450 --> 00:13:00,830
This is a completely new shot from Pierre.

219
00:13:01,240 --> 00:13:05,330
And at this moment, France makes it 1-1.

220
00:13:06,540 --> 00:13:10,080
Did you see? That's my jumping shot.

221
00:13:10,170 --> 00:13:12,590
- Pierre is great!
- Good luck, France!

222
00:13:12,920 --> 00:13:14,630
Jumping shot.

223
00:13:14,960 --> 00:13:16,090
This...

224
00:13:16,170 --> 00:13:18,510
You did it, Pierre, beautiful shot!

225
00:13:18,590 --> 00:13:20,300
What's your problem?

226
00:13:20,890 --> 00:13:23,350
Oh, the players clashed.

227
00:13:23,430 --> 00:13:25,890
They are Napoleon-kun and Soda-kun.

228
00:13:27,730 --> 00:13:29,560
End this, Soda.

229
00:13:29,650 --> 00:13:32,360
Players from both teams separate them.

230
00:13:32,480 --> 00:13:33,860
End this, Napoleon.

231
00:13:35,070 --> 00:13:39,360
It appears Napoleon-kun was fighting because of Soda-kun's tackle.

232
00:13:39,450 --> 00:13:42,870
But both were punished with yellow cards.

233
00:13:43,200 --> 00:13:44,540
Calm down, Soda.

234
00:13:44,620 --> 00:13:47,000
Both of them went overboard.

235
00:13:47,330 --> 00:13:48,540
Napoleon.

236
00:13:51,920 --> 00:13:53,000
What are you doing?

237
00:13:54,710 --> 00:13:56,260
Pierre.

238
00:13:58,380 --> 00:14:03,140
We didn't come here to have fun or fight.

239
00:14:03,390 --> 00:14:07,930
We are on this field for the honor of our homeland, for our own honor.

240
00:14:08,100 --> 00:14:10,060
And we do it in the most serious way.

241
00:14:10,480 --> 00:14:14,650
Football is a team sport where everyone plays together.

242
00:14:15,320 --> 00:14:18,150
I will not tolerate selfish behavior anymore.

243
00:14:18,400 --> 00:14:20,280
Do you understand, Napoleon?

244
00:14:20,910 --> 00:14:22,410
Pierre.

245
00:14:26,790 --> 00:14:31,250
El Sid Pierre, with those dribbles, shooting,

246
00:14:31,750 --> 00:14:34,170
and great attitude as a captain,

247
00:14:34,540 --> 00:14:36,550
it's clear what a magnificent player he is.

248
00:14:37,130 --> 00:14:38,880
Don't lose your cool, Soda.

249
00:14:38,970 --> 00:14:40,430
Yes, I know.

250
00:14:40,680 --> 00:14:46,810
Sorry guys, I was marking Pierre but I didn't know he had such a shot.

251
00:14:46,930 --> 00:14:49,060
No, it was my fault.

252
00:14:49,350 --> 00:14:51,190
I interfered with your job.

253
00:14:51,390 --> 00:14:53,650
What's done is done.

254
00:14:53,730 --> 00:14:54,690
Tsubasa.

255
00:14:54,940 --> 00:15:00,450
The game starts now. We'll score the second goal and get ahead of France.

256
00:15:00,530 --> 00:15:02,950
Right, Tsubasa is right.

257
00:15:03,160 --> 00:15:05,620
Alright, let's go and make up for the goal we conceded.

258
00:15:05,700 --> 00:15:06,700
Okay.

259
00:15:07,990 --> 00:15:12,790
Japan, who conceded the goal, kicks off.

260
00:15:16,420 --> 00:15:17,420
Let's advance.

261
00:15:17,500 --> 00:15:18,840
I'll get the ball!

262
00:15:19,210 --> 00:15:20,720
Let's go, Misaki-kun.

263
00:15:21,090 --> 00:15:22,340
Okay, Tsubasa-kun.

264
00:15:22,630 --> 00:15:23,800
Japan team.

265
00:15:23,890 --> 00:15:27,350
As usual, attacking with their Golden Duo Tsubasa-kun and Misaki-kun.

266
00:15:28,720 --> 00:15:29,680
That's it!

267
00:15:29,770 --> 00:15:35,100
With their masterful passing, they are demoralizing France, who just conceded the equalizer.

268
00:15:35,270 --> 00:15:38,110
This is Japan's Golden Duo.

269
00:15:38,900 --> 00:15:40,360
Their game...

270
00:15:40,490 --> 00:15:42,570
Well done, Tsubasa, Misaki.

271
00:15:42,650 --> 00:15:43,610
Advance!

272
00:15:44,160 --> 00:15:45,240
Taro.

273
00:15:45,740 --> 00:15:46,910
Tsubasa!

274
00:15:49,240 --> 00:15:50,120
Tsubasa!

275
00:15:50,290 --> 00:15:51,120
Alright!

276
00:15:51,200 --> 00:15:55,630
Oh, Tsubasa-kun receives the pass from Misaki-kun and takes his shot.

277
00:15:55,960 --> 00:15:58,000
Come on!

278
00:15:58,460 --> 00:16:00,510
Isn't this his special Drive Shot?

279
00:16:00,920 --> 00:16:03,840
No, its path is straight.

280
00:16:05,130 --> 00:16:06,260
I'll catch it.

281
00:16:07,300 --> 00:16:08,760
No, it drops straight down.

282
00:16:08,970 --> 00:16:10,010
What?

283
00:16:10,310 --> 00:16:12,640
This is just like Pierre's shot.

284
00:16:12,730 --> 00:16:15,270
This is Tsubasa-kun's jumping shot!

285
00:16:15,440 --> 00:16:16,270
What?

286
00:16:16,850 --> 00:16:19,860
Oh, but it hits the post!

287
00:16:20,610 --> 00:16:23,570
France cleared it and avoided a major danger.

288
00:16:23,820 --> 00:16:25,070
That was close.

289
00:16:25,150 --> 00:16:26,820
But that shot...

290
00:16:27,370 --> 00:16:30,240
Damn it, I didn't adjust it well.

291
00:16:30,490 --> 00:16:34,790
It wasn't a goal, but look once again, the Japanese football genius

292
00:16:34,870 --> 00:16:36,830
Ozora Tsubasa is incredible.

293
00:16:36,920 --> 00:16:41,340
He could imitate Pierre-kun's jumping shot after seeing it only once.

294
00:16:41,920 --> 00:16:43,840

295
00:16:44,510 --> 00:16:49,010
Impossible! I worked hard to perfect it.

296
00:16:49,100 --> 00:16:52,720
I wanted to keep my jumping shot for the final.

297
00:16:52,850 --> 00:16:54,480
How could he so easily...

298
00:16:54,980 --> 00:16:56,390
I thought.

299
00:16:56,480 --> 00:17:00,860
Drive Shot effect - Jumping shot effect - Smaller - Larger

300
00:16:56,810 --> 00:17:00,860
Just like in the Drive Shot, you give spin to the ball.

301
00:17:00,940 --> 00:17:05,780
Only in the jumping shot, you apply a hard forward pressure rather than spin.

302
00:17:05,950 --> 00:17:09,820
And it doesn't curve as much as the Drive Shot.

303
00:17:09,910 --> 00:17:12,490
However, it suddenly jumps and drops in front of the goalkeeper.

304
00:17:12,700 --> 00:17:13,870
I see.

305
00:17:13,950 --> 00:17:17,870
But you immediately understood and imitated it...

306
00:17:17,960 --> 00:17:19,460
Lizard, congratulations Tsubasa.

307
00:17:19,540 --> 00:17:22,500
I think they are still in shock.

308
00:17:23,210 --> 00:17:24,510
You haven't changed at all.

309
00:17:24,800 --> 00:17:31,260
You're still the old Tsubasa who makes the opponent's expertise your own.

310
00:17:33,770 --> 00:17:38,730
You hit the post and then made a comeback.

311
00:17:41,770 --> 00:17:44,190
I knew you'd come, Roberto.

312
00:17:45,440 --> 00:17:46,940
Coach Barbas.

313
00:17:47,110 --> 00:17:48,280
Hello.

314
00:17:48,400 --> 00:17:51,620
That shot could be a variation of the Drive Shot.

315
00:17:51,700 --> 00:17:55,950
Still, it's extraordinary that he made it his own after seeing it once.

316
00:17:56,040 --> 00:17:59,790
If he comes to Argentina, we will be great rivals.

317
00:18:01,130 --> 00:18:04,420
Coach Barbas, are you still thinking of taking Tsubasa to Argentina?

318
00:18:04,750 --> 00:18:08,420
Roberto, what happened between you two?

319
00:18:09,800 --> 00:18:12,600
If you don't mind, I'd like to know.

320
00:18:12,970 --> 00:18:14,930
Oh, Misaki-kun's father.

321
00:18:15,430 --> 00:18:16,680
Hello, kids.

322
00:18:16,890 --> 00:18:20,350
And the game restarts with a throw-in for Japan.

323
00:18:20,600 --> 00:18:21,440
Izawa.

324
00:18:21,730 --> 00:18:22,810
Misaki!

325
00:18:23,150 --> 00:18:24,440
Tsubasa-kun.

326
00:18:24,730 --> 00:18:28,280
Tsubasa-kun's jumping shot shocked the French.

327
00:18:28,360 --> 00:18:31,360
And it gave the advantage back to Japan.

328
00:18:31,450 --> 00:18:32,450
Hyuga-kun.

329
00:18:32,910 --> 00:18:35,740
And the ball goes toward Hyuga-kun in front of the goal.

330
00:18:36,200 --> 00:18:37,200
Nice.

331
00:18:37,370 --> 00:18:40,710
Get ready, I'm scoring the winning goal.

332
00:18:41,040 --> 00:18:41,960
Crush him!

333
00:18:42,040 --> 00:18:43,210
Stop him!

334
00:18:45,590 --> 00:18:47,210
Good, advance Hyuga.

335
00:18:47,300 --> 00:18:48,970
Good luck, Hyuga-san!

336
00:18:49,090 --> 00:18:51,970
Oh, Pierre-kun goes to block his path.

337
00:18:52,140 --> 00:18:52,970
What?

338
00:18:53,850 --> 00:18:56,470
Pierre-kun wins the ball.

339
00:18:56,850 --> 00:19:02,270
Japan's number 10, Ozora Tsubasa, you broke my pride.

340
00:19:02,520 --> 00:19:04,980
I'll make you experience ten times that.

341
00:19:05,440 --> 00:19:07,360
Pierre got serious.

342
00:19:07,690 --> 00:19:09,990
Pierre-kun starts dribbling.

343
00:19:10,190 --> 00:19:11,740
Misaki-kun goes to stop him.

344
00:19:12,200 --> 00:19:13,990
- Misaki!
- Pierre!

345
00:19:15,490 --> 00:19:16,740
Oh, this...

346
00:19:18,160 --> 00:19:20,830
Pierre-kun, the expert of elegant dribbling,

347
00:19:20,910 --> 00:19:23,790
now overpowered Misaki-kun using strength!

348
00:19:24,130 --> 00:19:27,130
That was a rough play and actually a foul.

349
00:19:27,300 --> 00:19:28,130
Misaki.

350
00:19:28,210 --> 00:19:30,760
Where are you looking, referee? He committed a foul.

351
00:19:30,880 --> 00:19:35,760
An opportunity for France. Will Pierre-kun take another jumping shot and score?

352
00:19:36,220 --> 00:19:38,260
Shoot, Pierre!

353
00:19:38,600 --> 00:19:40,770
I must catch this for Misaki-kun.

354
00:19:40,810 --> 00:19:42,980
Tsubasa-kun goes to stop him.

355
00:19:43,060 --> 00:19:45,270
Will Pierre-kun pass or dribble?

356
00:19:45,440 --> 00:19:48,610
He will dribble! Another attacking move.

357
00:19:48,690 --> 00:19:50,530
Tsubasa-kun makes a hard tackle.

358
00:19:51,530 --> 00:19:54,780
Oh, they collide at the same time.

359
00:19:54,950 --> 00:19:56,990
The ball separates!

360
00:19:58,410 --> 00:19:59,870
Catch, Napoleon.

361
00:19:59,950 --> 00:20:00,790
Damn it.

362
00:20:01,540 --> 00:20:03,540
This is a return pass.

363
00:20:05,460 --> 00:20:06,790
Good, this is a goal.

364
00:20:06,880 --> 00:20:07,960
Don't even dream of it.

365
00:20:08,040 --> 00:20:09,300
He will head it.

366
00:20:10,250 --> 00:20:12,800
They collide with each other in the air.

367
00:20:13,170 --> 00:20:15,800
Napoleon can't head it.

368
00:20:15,970 --> 00:20:18,550
Japan managed to defend.

369
00:20:18,640 --> 00:20:20,350
Great, Soda!

370
00:20:25,230 --> 00:20:28,310
Oh, a yellow card for Soda-kun.

371
00:20:28,610 --> 00:20:29,480
What?

372
00:20:31,360 --> 00:20:36,320
During the aerial duel, it appears Soda-kun's elbow hit Napoleon-kun's face.

373
00:20:36,990 --> 00:20:39,830
The referee judges it as intentional.

374
00:20:39,950 --> 00:20:43,120
This is Soda-kun's second yellow card today.

375
00:20:43,200 --> 00:20:44,330
He got a red card!

376
00:20:44,500 --> 00:20:47,580
Impossible! It wasn't intentional!

377
00:20:47,670 --> 00:20:49,590
Why am I being sent off?

378
00:20:49,750 --> 00:20:52,210
Soda didn't hit him on purpose.

379
00:20:52,300 --> 00:20:58,590
The Japan team protests, but the referee doesn't change the decision.

380
00:20:59,050 --> 00:21:01,140
The referee's decision is correct.

381
00:21:01,220 --> 00:21:03,100
Send him off.

382
00:21:03,310 --> 00:21:05,140
Only 10 minutes of the first half have passed.

383
00:21:05,230 --> 00:21:09,730
The Japan team must continue the rest of the match with 10 players.

384
00:21:10,060 --> 00:21:15,740
And this foul is inside the penalty area, France earned a penalty.

385
00:21:15,950 --> 00:21:19,240
This is not good for Japan.

386
00:21:19,490 --> 00:21:23,200
I didn't do anything to deserve being sent off.

387
00:21:23,290 --> 00:21:26,660
But Soda-kun is not leaving the field.

388
00:21:27,290 --> 00:21:28,250
Tsubasa!

389
00:21:30,250 --> 00:21:34,010
Referee, as the captain of the Japan team, I protest.

390
00:21:34,420 --> 00:21:37,510
I understand that you judged this action as a foul.

391
00:21:37,880 --> 00:21:42,010
But Soda-kun didn't do it intentionally, it was an accident.

392
00:21:42,390 --> 00:21:45,020
Please rescind the red card.

393
00:21:45,390 --> 00:21:47,390
Are you still protesting?

394
00:21:47,480 --> 00:21:49,650
The referee's decision is absolute.

395
00:21:49,900 --> 00:21:52,230
But it's clear that this is a wrong decision.

396
00:21:52,320 --> 00:21:53,150
Tsubasa-kun.

397
00:21:54,780 --> 00:21:57,900
Oh, and here is the third yellow card!

398
00:21:59,950 --> 00:22:05,870
A yellow card for Japan's captain Tsubasa-kun, who argued with the referee.

399
00:24:45,990 --> 00:24:49,950
Next episode: 10 vs 11